.TH SOFTWARE-FOUNDATION 7 "October 2026" "software-foundation 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
software-foundation \- installed application and developer package guide
.SH DESCRIPTION
This general-purpose reference separates application behavior, platform services,
GUI adapters, prepared build inputs and release verification.
The installed CLI demonstrates bounded input, failure atomicity and stable records.
.SH PACKAGE CONTENTS
.TP
.B bin/
Command-line executable and any selected native GUI hosts.
.TP
.B include/foundation/
Public C++ library interfaces and the package version.
.TP
.B lib/cmake/Foundation/
Installed CMake package configuration and imported targets.
Library directory spelling may follow the selected platform convention.
.TP
.B lib/runtime/
Private redistributable runtime dependencies, when required.
Host loaders and system services are not replacement package libraries.
.TP
.B share/doc/Foundation/
Notices, dependency inventory, build information and installed instructions.
.TP
.B share/man/
These manual pages. A manual reader is not needed to build or install them.
.TP
.B share/software-foundation/web/
Installed assets for enabled browser frontends.
.SH GUI FRONTENDS
Terminal, framebuffer, FLTK, Rev, SDL, hosted web and compiled WebAssembly hosts
consume the same application-owned widget definitions and event handling.
Enabled hosts are recorded in the package build information.
Adding an application feature through existing widget capabilities changes the
shared application definition. A new backend capability requires extending its
generic contract and conformance checks.
.PP
Native display backends require the corresponding host display services.
Browser frontends use an ordinary supported system browser. The compiler SDK
does not supply a desktop browser. Browser tests and compiler tools have separate
dependency and update policies.
.SH DEVELOPER USE
Use CMake find_package(Foundation CONFIG REQUIRED), link foundation::core,
and apply foundation_apply_runtime to the consuming target. Use a compiler,
runtime and target environment compatible with the recorded SDK.
A static library does not promise a compiler-independent binary interface.
.SH INSTALLATION AND REMOVAL
Extract portable archives into a new directory and keep all files together.
Run the packaged self-check outside the source checkout. Remove that complete
private directory to uninstall an archive; preserve user-owned data separately.
.PP
Use the native package manager to install and remove managed packages.
Backend variants occupy separate private installation directories. Their public
launchers and manual aliases identify the variant so several can coexist.
.SH RELEASE INPUTS
An application release retains the exact prepared SDK and dependency groups it
used, including source inputs, recipe identity and complete checksums.
Ordinary builds consume those retained inputs without downloading replacements.
SDK maintenance is a separate explicit operation. Qualification must test the
actual delivered archive and recovery when the original base is unavailable.
.SH SUPPORT EVIDENCE
The matching source release contains compatibility requirements, validation
records and the complete documentation index. A successful check on one host
does not qualify another operating system or processor. Consult the release's
actual evidence before relying on a declared target.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR foundation-cli (1)
